{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"SB0296","billNumberShort":"S.B. 296","billNumberLong":"SB0296S01","fileNumber":"2026FL1452","shortTitle":"Student Consent Amendments","currentSubVersion":"1","currentMinVersion":"3","primeSponsor":"CULLIKA","primeSponsorName":"Sen. Cullimore, Kirk A.","primeSponsorHouse":"S","floorSponsor":"GRICIS","floorSponsorName":"Rep. Gricius, Stephanie","floorSponsorHouse":"H","generalProvisions":"This bill enacts provisions related to a student's educational data and informed consent.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms;<hr><ltbullet>enacts certain rights regarding student data;<hr><ltbullet>requires an education entity and institution of higher education to:<hr><ltbullet1>disclose student data under certain circumstances;<hr><ltbullet1>offer a secure, digital mechanism for obtaining informed consent; and<hr><ltbullet1>follow certain procedures when obtaining a student's informed consent;<hr><ltbullet>allows an education entity and an institution of higher education to impose certain limitations;<hr><ltbullet>prohibits an education entity and an institution of higher education from:<hr><ltbullet1>restricting a student's ability to grant informed consent;<hr><ltbullet1>requiring a student to waive certain rights; or<hr><ltbullet1>imposing certain limitations on a student's informed consent;<hr><ltbullet>requires a parent to provide informed consent on behalf of the parent's minor student;<hr><ltbullet>creates a private right of action; and<hr><ltbullet>allows the State Board of Education and the Utah Board of Higher Education to issue best practices for informed consent.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Tyler Keetch","fiscalAnalyst":"Joseph Fitzgerald","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/19/2026","trackingID":"PBHWMSIXUN","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed"